a dimension of $3?$\n- **I.** ${R}^{2}$\n- **II.** ${R}_{2}[t]$, the vector space of all polynomials in the variable $t$ of degree at most $2$\n- **III.** ${\\text{M}}_{3}(R),$ the vector space of all $3\\times 3$ matrices over $R$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Let's examine each of the vector spaces in turn.\n\n- Recall that $\\text{dim}({R}^{n})=n.$ Therefore, \n\n$$\n\\text{dim}({R}^{2})=2\\ne 3.\\,\\times \n$$\n- Recall that $\\text{dim}({R}_{n}[t])=n+1.$ Therefore, \n\n$$\n\\text{dim}({R}_{2}[t])=2+1=3.\\,✓\n$$\n- Recall that $\\text{dim}({\\text{M}}_{n}(R))={n}^{2}.$ Therefore, \n\n$$\n\\text{dim}({\\text{M}}_{3}(R))={3}^{2}=9\\ne 3.\\,\\times \n$$\n\nHence, the correct answer is \"II only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186243977 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152220 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "aee17e3a-031d-5c0e-9488-17410b3a2372" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying True Statements About Dimensions of Vector Spaces"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "85f50e01-4432-5abc-a190-7e72cdc3873a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461479} {:answer/id #uuid "26b77efa-1ca5-50e3-a239-917ffd78fa11" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461480}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "85f50e01-4432-5abc-a190-7e72cdc3873a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461479} :answer-field/id #uuid "d618925b-ccec-5382-aafc-ee623f24eae3" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462493} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3755b38e-d3c3-5fd6-aa30-ce41d9c8f023" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461481} {:answer/id #uuid "0113c910-9d82-5496-a7a5-6245045c74c0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461482}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0113c910-9d82-5496-a7a5-6245045c74c0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461482} :answer-field/id #uuid "6af77266-4c24-5185-b7d2-41604c2df381" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462494} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e21d3928-a529-5423-a7ee-52349098e089" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461483} {:answer/id #uuid "a21066ee-90f4-5cd6-a2c8-b896111b61f8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461484}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a21066ee-90f4-5cd6-a2c8-b896111b61f8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461484} :answer-field/id #uuid "8e400bec-f914-5615-b660-6b8705f12fef" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462495}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "19d4d0ee-ad5b-53e7-956e-b02eb6cf177b" :question/math-academy-id "q-106901" :question/problem "Which of the following vector spaces has a dimension of $20?$\n- **I.** ${R}_{20}[t]$, the vector space of all polynomials in the variable $t$ of degree at most $20$\n- **II.** ${\\text{M}}_{4\\times 5}(R),$ the vector space of all $4\\times 5$ matrices over $R$\n- **III.** ${R}^{20}$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Let's examine each of the vector spaces in turn.\n\n- Recall that $\\text{dim}({R}_{n}[t])=n+1.$ Therefore, \n\n$$\n\\text{dim}({R}_{20}[t])=20+1=21\\ne 20.\\,\\times \n$$\n- Recall that $\\text{dim}({\\text{M}}_{n\\times m}(R))=n\\cdot m.$ Therefore, \n\n$$\n\\text{dim}({\\text{M}}_{4\\times 5}(R))=4\\cdot 5=20.\\,✓\n$$\n- Recall that $\\text{dim}({R}^{n})=n.$ Therefore, \n\n$$\n\\text{dim}({R}^{20})=20.\\,✓\n$$\n\nHence, the correct answer is \"II and III only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186484214 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152219 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "2a8bf202-99c5-5bfd-8df3-5bd27cd65640" :knowledge-point/title "Determining the Dimension of a Polynomial Vector Space Given Its Standard Monomial Basis"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "10a2070b-ee01-5111-a61c-4347e5d15c83" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "100" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186483595} {:answer/id #uuid "14be6a81-848a-5ae7-b43b-71982638b4f5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "10" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186483602} {:answer/id #uuid "71cae8a4-5a70-59fa-850b-21fa607637c3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "11" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186483791} {:answer/id #uuid "7427b7f3-6b05-5734-9feb-603f47022317" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "20" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186483800} {:answer/id #uuid "d039d520-3a75-55a1-9af7-a275fca2bb02" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186483986}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "71cae8a4-5a70-59fa-850b-21fa607637c3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "11" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186483791} :answer-field/id #uuid "1ae82675-ac3d-59f8-b4e1-4558ec943bfe" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186484094}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "3d3c2164-c9a8-58f5-b6ac-e24eb41f738f" :question/math-academy-id "q-95212" :question/problem "What is the dimension of ${R}_{10}[t]$, the vector space of all polynomials in the variable $t$ of degree at most $10?$" :question/worked-solution "The standard basis of ${R}_{n}[t]$ is\n\n$$\n\\{1,\\,t,\\,{t}^{2},\\,…,\\,{t}^{n}\\}.\n$$\n\nSo, the standard basis of ${R}_{10}[t]$ is \n\n$$\n\\{1,\\,t,\\,{t}^{2},\\,…,\\,{t}^{10}\\}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have that \n\n$$\n\\text{dim}({R}_{10}[t])=10+1=11.\n$$\n\nIn general,\n\n$$\n\\text{dim}({R}_{n}[t])=n+1.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186495107 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152220 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "aee17e3a-031d-5c0e-9488-17410b3a2372" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying True Statements About Dimensions of Vector Spaces"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2d9255a3-f808-53ab-9a1d-bce0b2aee8d7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186494406} {:answer/id #uuid "4ad4f74f-98bf-5d22-9457-443e51eb0e44" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186494468} {:answer/id #uuid "a6d9093c-41de-586e-8b9a-a4e06e3dceda" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186494702} {:answer/id #uuid "b2867c1c-1f11-5f60-8eeb-04a47f542fab" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I, II, and III" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186494734} {:answer/id #uuid "c9096bb1-9011-5dc6-aea5-546459a5a73c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186494790}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b2867c1c-1f11-5f60-8eeb-04a47f542fab" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I, II, and III" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186494734} :answer-field/id #uuid "7b5c8af9-d959-569a-8058-100af23b2c12" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186494973}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "872bbc86-b2d9-5fc0-a340-666aa227cedf" :question/math-academy-id "q-95225" :question/problem "Which of the following vector spaces has a dimension of $12?$\n\nI. ${R}^{12}$\n\nII. ${\\text{M}}_{3\\times 4}(R),$ the vector space of all $3\\times 4$ matrices over $R$\n\nIII. ${R}_{11}[t]$, the vector space of all polynomials in the variable $t$ of degree at most $11$" :question/worked-solution "Let's examine each of the vector spaces in turn.\n\nI. Recall that $\\text{dim}({R}^{n})=n.$ Therefore, \n\n  $$\n  \\text{dim}({R}^{12})=12.\\,✓\n  $$\n\nII. Recall that $\\text{dim}({\\text{M}}_{n\\times m}(R))=n\\cdot m.$ Therefore, \n\n  $$\n  \\text{dim}({\\text{M}}_{3\\times 4}(R))=3\\cdot 4=12.\\,✓\n  $$\n\nIII. Recall that $\\text{dim}({R}_{n}[t])=n+1.$ Therefore, \n\n  $$\n  \\text{dim}({R}_{11}[t])=11+1=12.\\,✓\n  $$\n\nHence, the correct answer is \"I, II, and III.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186495073 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152220 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "aee17e3a-031d-5c0e-9488-17410b3a2372" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying True Statements About Dimensions of Vector Spaces"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "32aca3cf-a5e2-53e0-9465-8c5812ddcb24" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186494418} {:answer/id #uuid "500ce576-4c92-5f17-8883-d14fb5dd6073" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186494479} {:answer/id #uuid "9317dd78-6bb1-51d8-9527-c7283331155e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186494653} {:answer/id #uuid "cab46aea-83c2-537f-b7c2-3ead6ff50e30" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186494797} {:answer/id #uuid "ce013736-d830-5648-bf13-13959d355826" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186494808}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "32aca3cf-a5e2-53e0-9465-8c5812ddcb24" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186494418} :answer-field/id #uuid "ae053587-50f1-5f8c-b674-29dc44c5f648" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186494998}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "300def0f-69c7-5821-80a9-ead2c4071d95" :question/math-academy-id "q-95228" :question/problem "Which of the following vector spaces has a dimension of $18?$\n\nI. ${R}_{17}[t]$, the vector space of all polynomials in the variable $t$ of degree at most $17$\n\nII. ${\\text{M}}_{6\\times 3}(R),$ the vector space of all $6\\times 3$ matrices over $R$\n\nIII. ${R}^{17}$" :question/worked-solution "Let's examine each of the vector spaces in turn.\n\nI. Recall that $\\text{dim}({R}_{n}[t])=n+1.$ Therefore, \n\n  $$\n  \\text{dim}({R}_{17}[t])=17+1=18.\\,✓\n  $$\n\nII. Recall that $\\text{dim}({\\text{M}}_{n\\times m}(R))=n\\cdot m.$ Therefore, \n\n  $$\n  \\text{dim}({\\text{M}}_{6\\times 3}(R))=6\\cdot 3=18.\\,✓\n  $$\n\nIII. Recall that $\\text{dim}({R}^{n})=n.$ Therefore, \n\n  $$\n  \\text{dim}({R}^{17})=17\\ne 18.\\,\\times \n  $$\n\nHence, the correct answer is \"I and II only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152876 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152221 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "e609aabf-7e7e-5997-b8dc-c66e7a14a36f" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Finite and Infinite-Dimensional Vector Spaces"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8e0d7093-d23a-56ed-9ebe-e8cae0bf1583" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186151764} {:answer/id #uuid "9332984e-d4f3-5c83-9c85-15c6b80b05e8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186151765} {:answer/id #uuid "085d9ff6-4647-5320-8166-7fd2905e1855" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186151766} {:answer/id #uuid "1b11fc68-6513-585b-957a-6e0ea33524a4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I, II, and III" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186151767} {:answer/id #uuid "4ef66779-081f-5eda-82b4-3ed4176bc616" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186151768}] :answer-field/id #uuid "b408dce0-ca2d-5ac0-810c-dcc878bc60db" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186151763}] :question/id #uuid "2a7f694e-9eb9-56c4-8f1f-0236761451e0" :question/math-academy-id "q-95236" :question/problem "Which of the following vector spaces are finite-dimensional?\n\n1. $ℓ^{2}$, the vector space of infinite real sequences where the sum of the squares of the terms are finite\n2. $R_{2}[t]$, the vector space of all polynomials in the variable $t$ of degree at most $2$\n3. $M_{100 \\cdot 1000}(R)$, the vector space of all $100 \\cdot 1000$ matrices over $R$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186360589 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152221 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "e609aabf-7e7e-5997-b8dc-c66e7a14a36f" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Finite and Infinite-Dimensional Vector Spaces"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "bfb76c40-7724-5451-8aac-19d2a8b57bd1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469752} {:answer/id #uuid "c8f44b9f-b85e-5529-ac9f-fe0670b28b81" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469753}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c8f44b9f-b85e-5529-ac9f-fe0670b28b81" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469753} :answer-field/id #uuid "73b049e3-3f6a-5ae0-9695-c15b320edad7" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470488} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0bbe85bc-6a5b-5101-83b8-3cbc7f9dadf7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469754} {:answer/id #uuid "6ab4000e-252f-55bb-ae53-9aff79c28b25" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469755}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0bbe85bc-6a5b-5101-83b8-3cbc7f9dadf7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469754} :answer-field/id #uuid "a4771de7-dcbb-5f3d-b4f0-14014f000a86" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470489} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "725da332-7f7a-56cd-b1c7-eb7e1e678523" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469756} {:answer/id #uuid "72759b00-fedb-5a37-ab83-88c976d1613c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469757}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "72759b00-fedb-5a37-ab83-88c976d1613c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469757} :answer-field/id #uuid "bd7d2395-b54b-5c6b-a214-dab27c08b450" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470490}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "9ccb2591-5640-5714-9681-7f41d3b4bf27" :question/math-academy-id "q-95239" :question/problem "Which of the following vector spaces are finite-dimensional?\n- **I.** ${R}^{200}$\n- **II.** $R[t],$ the vector space of all polynomial functions in the variable $t$\n- **III.** ${\\text{M}}_{200}(R),$ the vector space of all $200\\times 200$ matrices over $R$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Let's examine our vector spaces.\n\n- $R[t]$ is *not* finite-dimensional. To understand why, we first note that the following set of (polynomial) functions is linearly independent:\n\n$$\n{1,\\,t,\\,{t}^{2},\\,…,{t}^{n}},\\,n\\in N.\n$$\n\nIndeed, we have that \n\n$$\n{\\sum }_{i=0}^{n}{a}_{i}{t}^{i}=0\n$$\n\nfor all $t\\in R$ if and only if ${a}_{i}=0$ for all $i=0,1,2,…,n.$ Therefore,  for any  $n\\in N,$  there exists a linearly independent subset of $R[t]$ of size $n,$ which imples that $R[t]$ cannot have finite dimension.\n\n- ${\\text{M}}_{200}(R)$ and ${R}^{200}$ are finite-dimensional. Indeed, \n\n$$\n\\text{dim}({\\text{M}}_{200}(R))={200}^{2}=40\\,000,\n$$\n\n \nand\n\n$$\n\\text{dim}({R}^{200})=200\n$$\n\nare both finite numbers.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and III only.\""}]}
